LICENCE OF THIS REPOSITORY
--------------------------

The Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE) covers the code and the text
written for this repository: the method specifications, prompts, scripts,
checks, reports, the error ledger, the manuscript source and the release
tools.

Some files are copies or subsets of public resources, or contain values
taken from them. Those files keep the licence and terms of their source.
The Apache licence does not replace them. This applies both to the files in
the git repository and to the files kept on Zenodo (ZENODO_MANIFEST.csv).

The list below names each kind of third-party file, where it is in this
repository, and its source. Where the source states a licence, it is given
with the page it was read from (read on 4 October 2026). Where we could not
confirm a licence, the entry says "see the source". Check the source before
any reuse, in particular any commercial reuse.

Some of the files named below are over 2 MB and are kept on Zenodo, not in
git; ZENODO_MANIFEST.csv lists them. DATASETS.md, CHECKPOINTS.md and
DATASETS_EVAL_INPUTS.csv give versions, sizes and sha256 values. Each study
package's README.md says how its data files were made.

The Study C snapshot (controlled-evaluation/studyC/snapshot/) is kept on
Zenodo, in files_eval_studyC.zip. It holds the project files that the blind
auditors received. Most of them are copies of files under projects/maxtoki/
in this repository, and the entries below cover those copies too. It also
holds copies of MaxToki setup files (see MaxToki in section 1).

The snapshot that the auditors received also held six third-party
reference files. These six are not deposited on Zenodo. They were in the
folder
controlled-evaluation/studyC/snapshot/maxtoki/reference_data/biomechinterp/biodyn-nmi-paper/:
  - results/biological_impact/reference_edge_sets/go_bp_gene_sets.json
    (GO biological process gene sets)
